      "parameters": {
        "mode": "retrieve-as-tool",
        "toolDescription": "=Search the company's internal knowledge base in Qdrant to retrieve accurate, relevant information that answers the AI Agent's question.\n\nInstructions:\n1. Search the stored documents for information directly related to the user's query.\n2. Retrieve the most relevant document chunks, including related information that provides useful context.\n3. Use the retrieved information to answer questions about the company's background, products, services, pricing, policies, procedures, and operations.\n4. Prioritise factual information explicitly stated in the internal documents. Do not invent, assume, or fabricate information.\n5. If the query uses different wording from the documents, identify semantically similar information rather than relying only on exact keyword matches.\n6. If relevant information is found across multiple document chunks, retrieve and use all relevant context available.\n7. If the knowledge base does not contain sufficient information, clearly indicate that the information could not be verified from the internal documents.\n8. Return the retrieved information with its original meaning preserved. Do not generate an answer unrelated to the retrieved documents.\n\nYour objective is to retrieve the most relevant and reliable internal company information so the AI Agent can provide accurate, evidence-based answers.",
